===Etymology===
After {{w|Ebola river}} (area of discovery of type species) {{suffix|mul||virus|nocat=1}}. Reports conflict about who initially coined the name: either Karl Johnson of the American Centers for Disease Control<ref name="hz">{{cite-book|title={{w|The Hot Zone}}|last=Preston|first=Richard|author={{w|Richard Preston}}|page=117|text=Karl Johnson named it Ebola|publisher=Anchor Books ([[Random House]])|date=July 20, 1995}}</ref> or Belgian researchers.<ref name="observer">{{cite-web|url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/oct/04/ebola-zaire-peter-piot-outbreak|title='In 1976 I Discovered Ebola&nbsp;– Now I Fear an Unimaginable Tragedy'|last1=Bredow|first1=Rafaela von|last2=Hackenbroch|first2=Veronika|work=[[The Observer]]|publisher=[[Guardian Media Group]]|date=4 October 2014}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Any extremely contagious [[filovirus]] infection of African origin that causes [[Ebola fever]], spread through contact with bodily fluids or secretions of infected persons and by airborne particles, caused by the viruses in genus ''[[Ebolavirus]]''.

